[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to find the largest possible real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m Substituting \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m = 4(75 + 117i)(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m = 4[(75 + 117i)(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)] + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m = 4[(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)] + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m To simplify the second term, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m = \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4} = 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m 4[(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)] + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta + i(4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m = (300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta) + i(276\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta\). To find the maximum value of this expression, we can use the method of finding the amplitude of a sinusoidal function. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta - b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = 468\), so the maximum value is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 468^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 219024} = \sqrt{324000} = 570
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=418378)[0m So the largest possible real part of the expression is \(\boxed{570}\).
